   the planet's children need to be listened to on issues pertaining to the
   environment, nature and Environmental Education. To this end, we propose
   a dialog between Environmental Education and children, specifically in
   early childhood education, from the perspective of the Sociology of and
   articulated with the Bioecological Theory of Human Development. The
   research is bibliographical and qualitative in nature. We found that in
   early childhood education, by giving children the opportunity to
   interact freely with nature and the environment in which they live, and
   by respecting their immediate surroundings and, ultimately, the planet,
   our shared home.},
